# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads as the build context.
#
# Without this file gcloud derives one from .gitignore, which covers node_modules and dist but says
# nothing about `.claude/` — and the agent worktrees under it are full copies of the repository,
# well over a gigabyte. They are not merely wasted upload time: each one carries its own
# cloudbuild.yaml, Dockerfile and drizzle/ directory, so a stray path in a build step could read a
# stale copy of the thing it is supposed to be building.
#
# Kept deliberately: apps/api/drizzle (the migration SQL the runtime image copies beside dist/) and
# every workspace manifest, since the Dockerfile installs from the lockfile at the repo root.

.git/
.gitignore

# Agent worktrees — stale duplicates of this repository.
.claude/

node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
.turbo/
**/.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Never upload a local environment file. The build has no use for one and the image must not
# contain it; production values come from Secret Manager.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
